The kinetic theory based functions \(\eta_{D}\), \(\kappa_{\parallel}\), \(\kappa_{\perp}\), and \(\kappa_{z}\) describe the momentum loss as well as fluctuations (transverse and longitudinal). They are given as Eqs. 2.3.

